  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The wire kerf law reads a signed clearance (`dist::entry` in `crates/sim/src/verify/wire/dist.rs`).\n- A move that stands in the product reads minus the distance from its deepest point to the product's boundary.\n- The gouge depth is the kerf reach plus that distance.\n- The closed-cut law (`passes::gouge_at`) and the open-run law (`kerf::gouge_at`) use it.\n- The threading law and the open-end law keep the unsigned `clearance`. They need only \"clear or not\".\n- The verdict does not change. Each move that gouged before still gouges, and the post stays blocked.\n\n## Cause\n\n`dist::clearance` returns 0 when a move stands in the product. The reading was then `need - 0`, the kerf offset. Thus each gouge with the wire centre inside the part said 0.162 mm, also for an entry of 2.8 mm.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/sim/src/verify/wire/depth_tests.rs`. The walls lean by 2.84 mm over 20 mm. The wire is cut at the Z0 offset. The depth is known in closed form.\n\n- `a_punch_whose_walls_lean_out_says_the_wall_shift_as_the_depth`: 1.42 mm at Z10, deepest 2.84 mm at Z20. Red before the fix (read 0.162).\n- `a_die_opening_that_narrows_says_the_corner_entry`: the issue's lofted opening (10.34 to 7.5). Move 1 reads 1.42 mm at Z10. The deepest reading is at the Z20 corner: `sqrt(2) * (2.84 - k) + k`. Red before the fix (read 0.162).\n- `an_open_run_along_a_leaning_wall_says_the_wall_shift_as_the_depth`: the same readings on an open run.\n- `a_kerf_that_only_grazes_the_part_still_reads_its_entry`: a wire centre outside the part reads `k - clearance`, as before. Green before and after.\n\nMutations:\n\n- `kerf.rs` call site back to `clearance`: the open-run pin is red. Restored: green.\n- `passes.rs` call site back to `clearance`: the punch and die pins are red. Restored: green.\n\nGate on head 5c56d217f, all green:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 7 steps, 0 failed (sim lib, app `solid_law_goldens`, `wire_burnout`, `wire_tabs`, `wire_taper`, `wire_verify`).\n- `cargo xtask gate test a_tessellated_loft --crate app --binary wire_verify_tol`: ok. This test parses the deepest reading.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real lofted STEP part through MCP. The pins use synthetic square sections.\n- The deepest point on a move is found by a walk of 33 points, then 33 points around the best one. The error is below 1/1024 of the move length. A move end is always read exactly.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/sim/src/verify/wire/`.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3211-wire-gouge-depth.md`.\n\nChangelog: The wire EDM gouge refusal now says how deep the kerf enters the part, not the kerf offset, when the wire stands inside the part.\n\nFixes #3211\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
